## E. EVIDENCE GAPS AND RESEARCH NEEDS

| Evidence Gap | Priority | Why It Matters |
|-------------|----------|---------------|
| **Optimal virtual ward patient selection criteria** | 5 | Current evidence is condition-specific; broader medical admission virtual ward evidence is weak. Large pragmatic RCT needed in NHS context |
| **Discharge-to-Assess outcomes in high-complexity patients** | 10 | Evidence largely from less complex older adults; frail patients with severe dementia or high nursing needs are underrepresented in D2A trials |
| **Long-term outcomes of SDEC for older adults** | 4 | Most SDEC evidence excludes or underrepresents patients with frailty and multimorbidity — the dominant NHS winter admission population |
| **Cost-effectiveness of integrated care/ICS model** | 10 | Despite policy investment, robust economic evidence for ICS-level integration outcomes in the NHS is limited |
| **Implementation fidelity of HELP delirium prevention** | 7 | RCT evidence is strong but real-world implementation in under-resourced NHS wards is poorly studied; volunteer recruitment is a critical unknown |
| **RSV vaccination real-world effectiveness in NHS population** | 1 | RENOIR trial evidence was from a relatively healthy trial population; real-world NHS evidence for the 2024 programme is needed urgently |
| **Equity impact of virtual ward programmes** | 5 | No published RCT data on outcomes stratified by deprivation in NHS virtual ward programmes |
| **Care home clinical support (EHCH) full health economic modelling** | 9 | NHS EHCH evaluation exists but is not powered for full economic analysis; observational data only |
| **Predictive modelling for respiratory surge** | 8 | No validated real-time model has been prospectively evaluated in the English NHS context for operational accuracy |
| **Anticholinergic burden reduction and delirium outcomes** | 7 | Observational associations are strong, but RCT evidence for ACB reduction preventing delirium in acute admissions is limited |
| **Community COPD management telerehabilitation versus face-to-face** | 3 | Growing evidence but insufficient long-term follow-up data particularly for severe COPD and deprived groups |
| **Patient activation and social prescribing for ACSC reduction** | 3 | Promising mechanism but few high-quality RCTs demonstrating ACSC admission reduction specifically |

